"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"When you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, p5r.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder inside the Archipelago Launcher directory. Then, the mod manager (Reloaded-II) and its dependencies will then be installed inside the game's Steam folder inside a new 'Reloaded-II' folder. The AP Mod folder will be downloaded inside 'Reloaded-II\\Mods'.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"P5R is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file. When 'p5r.apworld' is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once everything is set up, open 'Reloaded-II.exe' (can be open automatically by setting up using the launch after setup toggle), click the '+' icon on the left bar and select your P5R executable (P5R.exe). Now, click the newly added 'Persona 5 Royal' app on the left bar and in the mod list add 'P5R Archipelago'. Then, click the P5R Archipelago mod once and go to 'Configure Mod'.\n\nIn 'Save Directory' select any directory, it doesn't matter.\n\nIn the 'Server Address' field, enter archipelago.gg: followed by the port. This is a 5-digit number that you can find on the website after creating a new room.\n\nThe 'Server Password' field is optional. If the host did not set one, leave it blank.\n\nIn 'Slot Name', enter the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nYou can also change some options there.\n\nFinally, once you're done, click 'Save', close the config window and press 'Launch Application' on the left and you should be connected and ready to play!",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
"You have 2 revert options, both can't be enabled at the same time.\n\nIf you use the 'Clear AP Mods' option it will only delete the mods that are required for P5R Archipelago.\n\nIf you use the 'Full Clear' option it will delete everything related to Reloaded-II and its mods. If other mods are detected an additionnal confirmation will appear.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] PopTracker Infos",
"kill",
"Some games have a PopTracker integration for Archipelago which allows you to track all possible Locations, Items, Upgrades, Zones, Hints and more depending on the game.\n\nFor the setup there are 3 different cases:\n\n\t• If the selected directory does not contain a PopTracker folder (or any similarly named folder), a new 'poptracker' folder will be created and the pack will be downloaded to poptracker\\packs.\n\n\t• If the selected directory already contains a folder with 'PopTracker' in its name, the installer will look for a poptracker.exe file. If one is found, the pack will be downloaded to its packs folder. If no poptracker.exe is found, the folder will be renamed to 'poptracker' and any missing files or folders will be created.\n\n\t• If the selected directory is already a PopTracker folder (for example: C:\\Users\\magni\\Documents\\poptracker), its contents will be validated. If everything is present, the pack will simply be downloaded to poptracker\\packs. Otherwise, the folder will be repaired before the pack is installed.",
